The dca crate declares Apache-2.0, but describes itself as a native Rust port of FFmpeg's DTS
decoder. Its core, XLL, EXSS, synthesis and header parsing code name the FFmpeg files below as
their sources, and its tables are generated from FFmpeg's dcadata.c and dcahuff.c. Those files are
licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1 or (at your option) any later
version (LGPL-2.1). Combined with the crate's Apache-2.0 code, the crate can be used under version 3
or later of that license (LGPL-3.0), whose text incorporates the GNU General Public License,
version 3 (GPL-3.0).

